Constructor


	1 .PHP allows you to declare a constructor method for a class with the name __construct()


		class ClassName
		{
			function __construct()
			{
				// implementation
			}
		}


	2. When you create an instance of the class, PHP automatically calls the constructor


		$object = new ClassName()

	3. Typically, you use the constructor to initialize the properties of the object.



	PHP constructor promotion 

	1.In practice, you often need to assign the constructor arguments to corresponding properties. It’s kind of redundant.



		class BankAccount
		{
			function __construct( private $accountNumber, private $balance)
			{	
			}
		}



	PHP constructor is a special method that is called automatically when an object is created.
	Do use constructor promotion as much as possible to make the code shorter.

Destructor

	

	1. PHP destructor and use it to clean up the resources when the object is deleted.

	2. special method __destruct() like this:


		<?php

			class className
			{
				public function __destruct()
				{
					//...
				}
			}

	3. The destructor is automatically invoked before an object is deleted.